  "description": "Borg explicitly uses FastCDC fastcdc,19,23,21,2, LZ4, authenticated unencrypted storage and metadata-based resume. Gutch uses a nominal 2 MiB FastCDC target, LZ4 0 and 8 MiB compressed bundles. Bounds, hashes, compression framing and storage layout differ. Borg cannot detect preserved-mtime damage via resume and this adapter has no native extra-file cleanup. Fresh repositories and isolated caches. Four workers where exposed; native Borg/BPT scheduling. One warm-up and 6 rotating measured repetitions; profiling off. Measurement contract 2 separates content repair, preserved-mtime damage, extra-file cleanup and full restoration. Strict source-derived SHA-256 validation follows every supported operation; both native and validation-inclusive durations are reported. Unsupported operations receive no timing.",
